/-!
# Finite configurations for the first large-ratio case

The last two signed columns each have six possibilities, with sums 1 and -1.
For any selected large-ratio constituent, its residue and absolute degree bound
leave 25 possible quotient positions. The table below deduplicates those
possibilities and gives a bound on the next signed degree. Both coverage of the
table and every bound are checked by kernel reduction.

For each resulting bounded pair of degrees, the third degree follows from
the degree-zero relation and the ambient order from the Suzuki equation.
The final kernel check tests the necessary denominator divisibility, degree
divisibility and cofactor conditions. No group order bound is assumed.

Source: Z. Janko, *A characterization of the Mathieu simple groups, I*,
J. Algebra 9 (1968), Section 7, pp.14–15. This supplies the omitted exhaustive
arithmetic, extending the printed degree-44 example.
-/

